WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Real work draws on more than one kind of energy.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.675
Physical energy supports movement, presence, and basic stamina.

00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:10.600
Cognitive energy supports analysis, memory, planning, and complex decision-making.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.000
Emotional energy supports patience, restraint, empathy,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.900
and the ability to handle friction without escalating it.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.180
Social energy supports collaboration, communication, facilitation,

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.970
and relationship maintenance.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.475
Creative energy is the capacity to make something new or solve a problem from an angle

00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:26.298
that is not obvious yet.

00:00:26.298 --> 00:00:29.940
Decision energy supports choices when the answer is uncertain, tradeoffs are real,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.275
and consequences matter.

00:00:31.275 --> 00:00:33.600
These capacity pools overlap, but they are not identical.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.005
A person may be physically rested and still depleted from difficult decisions.

00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:42.165
Another person may have social energy but not enough cognitive room for deep analysis.

00:00:42.165 --> 00:00:43.935
Different work types create different demands.

00:00:43.935 --> 00:00:45.955
Meetings draw on social and decision energy,

00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:48.280
especially if they involve conflict or ambiguity.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.840
Deep work draws heavily on cognitive energy and sustained attention.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.544
Troubleshooting combines focus, memory, patience, and judgment.

00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:58.400
Learning requires attention and enough humility to tolerate not knowing yet.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.970
Administrative work may seem small,

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.740
but constant small tasks can still drain capacity through fragmentation.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.760
Fatigue does not always announce itself directly.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.700
It can show up as procrastination, irritability, shallow work, careless judgment,

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.450
repeated checking, avoidance of hard conversations,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.435
or a tendency to choose the easiest visible task.

00:01:15.435 --> 00:01:17.110
Before assuming a motivation problem,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.810
it is worth asking what kind of energy the work requires and whether that kind of capacity

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:21.830
is actually available.
